\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Historical survey execution: trajectory-linked camera views from the accepted corrected \texttt  {validation\_002} task with an 80\% inspectable-coverage goal. Views 1--5 link locally to the radial--cross-track ($x$--$z$) projection, and views 6--10 link to the along-track--cross-track ($y$--$z$) projection; hollow gray markers retain the other observations as context. Inset labels give mission time and cumulative coverage. Dashed gray and solid blue denote planned and executed paths, and the star is the initial state. Clearance is evaluated against the full 3-D mesh and swept path. Gazebo renders the views, ROS HCW dynamics propagate state, and frozen geometric visibility masks determine credited coverage.}}{11}{figure.95}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ros-key-camera-views}{{7}{11}{Historical survey execution: trajectory-linked camera views from the accepted corrected \texttt {validation\_002} task with an 80\% inspectable-coverage goal. Views 1--5 link locally to the radial--cross-track ($x$--$z$) projection, and views 6--10 link to the along-track--cross-track ($y$--$z$) projection; hollow gray markers retain the other observations as context. Inset labels give mission time and cumulative coverage. Dashed gray and solid blue denote planned and executed paths, and the star is the initial state. Clearance is evaluated against the full 3-D mesh and swept path. Gazebo renders the views, ROS HCW dynamics propagate state, and frozen geometric visibility masks determine credited coverage}{figure.95}{}}
